        "like": 6
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I hate to say this, but I think with the VRC team's lack of response to our criticisms over the past week (and the news that they sneakily tried using an AI image for the login screen before taking it down and acting like nothing happened), It's likely that they've already heard our outcry and have chosen to ignore it. There is a decent chance that they are not on our side with this, and that possibility depresses me greatly.\n\nI've been a supporter of this platform for a long time, for the better part of a decade now. It's held a special place in my heart, and I've put my all into making content for it... It all just feels like a spit in the face to see the signs of the direction VRChat might be going in now. \n\nHere I was, actively financially supporting this platform and making content for it, wishing for its success... but now I'm seeing the price of that. If the price for success is the platform losing its very identity, then you can count me out. There has to be another way that doesn't involve caving under the pressure of people who parade around technology that steals from people without their consent.\n\nI apologize for the wall of text, but this is an issue I'm deeply passionate on. I'll be following this situation closely and I'm still holding out hope that there can be some change... but if things continue to go the way they're going, then I'll be halting all my support for VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
